# Front-office SEO (Inertia + Vue)

End-user pages use **Laravel + Inertia.js + Vue 3**. SEO must appear in **View Page Source** (first HTML) and stay correct after SPA navigations.

Inertia SSR is **optional** (`INERTIA_SSR_ENABLED` defaults to `false`). Do **not** rely on SSR for document meta — use the Blade + Vue dual-write below.

## Dual-write mental model

> **View Page Source = first Laravel HTML** (`app.blade.php`).  
> **Inspect = DOM after JavaScript.**  
>  
> If SEO must be visible in source, put it in Blade (via `$seo` / `withViewData`).  
> If SEO must survive SPA navigations, also put it in Inertia `<Head>` with matching `head-key`.  
> Do both.

```
Browser request
  → Laravel renders app.blade.php   ←── View Page Source (title/meta with inertia="")
  → Vue / Inertia hydrates
  → <Head head-key="…"> updates     ←── Inspect / SPA navigations
```

## Where global SEO lives

| Layer | Location |
|-------|----------|
| PHP resolver | `Modules\Base\Application\Seo\SeoDocumentService::documentSeo()` |
| Default Blade data | `View::composer('app')` in `AppServiceProvider` |
| Server-rendered tags | `resources/views/app.blade.php` (`inertia="description"` etc.) |
| Shared Inertia props | `HandleInertiaRequests` → `page.props.globals.seo` / `media` / `appName` |
| Vue hub helper | `resources/js/composables/useDocumentSeo.js` |

`HandleInertiaRequests` still shares:

| Key | Purpose |
|-----|--------|
| `globals.seo` | Localized key/value rows from `Modules\Base\Models\Seo` |
| `globals.media` | Resolved public URLs, including `meta_img` |
| `globals.about` / `turkish_citizenship` | Section copy + meta fields |

## Blade + `withViewData` (required for View Source)

Every public `Inertia::render` should pass page-specific SEO when the title/description differs from site defaults:

```php
return Inertia::render('…', $props)
    ->withViewData([
        'seo' => app(SeoDocumentService::class)->documentSeo([
            'page_title' => 'Catalogue', // → "Catalogue | Site Name"
            // or 'title' => full string for entity pages
            'description' => '…',
            'keywords' => '…',
            'og_image' => '…',
            'canonical' => route('…'),
            'og_type' => 'website', // or 'article'
            'robots' => 'noindex, nofollow', // auth / favorites
        ]),
    ]);
```

`SeoDocumentService` fallbacks (when overrides empty):

- **Title:** `site_meta_title` → `main_title` → `website_name` → `config('app.name')`
- **With `page_title`:** `"{page_title} | {siteName}"` (skip append if already contains site name)
- **Description / keywords:** `site_meta_*` → `website_desc` / `website_keywords`
- **og_image:** settings `meta_img` (via media resolver)

Root Blade emits `<title inertia>`, `<meta inertia="description">`, keywords, OG, canonical — matching Vue `head-key` values so Inertia replaces nodes instead of duplicating them.

## Page tiers (convention)

### 1) Global / hub pages

**Examples:** Home, property listings index, blog index, Contact Us.

- Blade: `documentSeo()` defaults or `page_title` + canonical.
- Vue: `useDocumentSeo({ useGlobalTitleTemplate: true })` (home) or `pageTitle: …`.

### 2) Parent / section pages

**Examples:** About Us, Turkish citizenship.

- Prefer section meta keys, then site fallbacks.
- Controllers pass `page_title` / `description_keys` / section banner as `og_image`.

### 3) Detail pages (single entity)

**Examples:** Property show, blog show, CMS page.

- Title/description/keywords/og_image/canonical from **entity** props — also via `withViewData` so social crawlers see them without JS.
- Vue `<Head>` stays entity-driven; keep `head-key` aligned with Blade.

## Vue `<Head>` checklist

1. Import `Head` from `@inertiajs/vue3`.
2. Prefer `useDocumentSeo` on hubs; details keep entity computeds.
3. Use **`head-key`** matching Blade `inertia="…"`: `description`, `keywords`, `canonical`, `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image`, `og:type`, `og:url`, `robots`.
4. Canonical via Ziggy `route(...)` / localized helpers — no hard-coded production domains.
5. `createInertiaApp({ title })` is a **pass-through** (pages already send full `"Label | Site"` titles). Do not double-append the site name.

## Verification

1. Full reload (not only SPA click) → **View Page Source** has `<title>`, `meta name="description"`, keywords.
2. Inspect shows the same tags after hydrate.
3. Inertia link away and back — Head still updates.
4. Feature tests assert **raw HTML** (`assertSee(..., false)`), not only Inertia props.

